# Recovery & maintenance scripts

Applies to `scripts/*.py`. See [docs/data-recovery.md](../../docs/data-recovery.md) for the full recovery workflow.

## Conventions

- **Dry-run by default** — print planned actions; gate real writes behind `--apply`
- **Never hard-delete** — move to quarantine/archive or Immich soft-trash; log skips
- **Stdlib-first** — `organize_recovery.py` has no third-party deps; only add deps when necessary (e.g. `mutagen` in `reorganize_music.py`)
- **Docstring usage block** — keep `Usage:` examples in the module docstring current when CLI changes

## Script roles

| Script | Runs on | Notes |
| ------ | ------- | ----- |
| `organize_recovery.py` | Mac (external volumes) | scan / merge-dupes / transfer pipeline |
| `reorganize_music.py` | NAS or Mac | writes to sibling `music_organized` tree |
| `queue_watch.py` | Mac | SSH to `igorbot.local`, local history file |
| `build_albums.py` | NAS | localhost Immich API + transfer log |
| `archive_cleanup.py` | NAS | Immich soft-trash after verified archive copy |

## Verification

```bash
python3 -m py_compile scripts/<changed>.py
```

Dry-run the affected subcommand before suggesting `--apply`.
